    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "36a829a2_dd0bab06",
        "filename": "common/charge_ramp.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1103909
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-02-12T03:01:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "i\u0027m not sure what the benefit of limiting at a lower value would be, but i can tell you 10/16 chargers we\u0027ve tested go above 2A.",
      "parentUuid": "3644a9e8_9d15033b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "15514d4db3e51523aee2e62b5b45d92d1263697b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d61c2dfd_fa10c94b",
        "filename": "common/charge_ramp.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000094
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-02-12T03:32:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But are those chargers rated above 2A? Are the contacts on their USB connectors rated for above 2A (probably not, unless they are designed for USB-PD)? Could we do bad things to them by pulling too much current (overheat for example)?",
      "parentUuid": "36a829a2_dd0bab06",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "15514d4db3e51523aee2e62b5b45d92d1263697b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9664759b_0889c739",
        "filename": "common/charge_ramp.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001139
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-02-12T07:18:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Then why 2A? If we lower this to 2A, the same questions stand for 1.5A. Unless the spec requires the cables and the connectors to support 2A?",
      "parentUuid": "d61c2dfd_fa10c94b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "15514d4db3e51523aee2e62b5b45d92d1263697b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9664759b_680de3ad",
        "filename": "common/charge_ramp.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000094
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-02-12T17:05:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correct, the connector is speced at 2A (per USB spec for an A connector the test is at 1.8A for a B at 2A, but in practice everyone uses 2A -- we looked at this a lot in the Yoshi days). That is why the Yoshi power adapter had to be a captive cable, because we had to ensure a 3A rated plug was used.\n\nThe other argument for 2A vs 1.5A is based on what is observed: from what power adapters do everyone is comfortable using up to 2A. But the higher current ones (like iPAD) have a proprietary connector on one end of the cable, so can ensure the connectors are rated. We are ok there because we detect the proprietary signature so no need to ramp.",
      "parentUuid": "9664759b_0889c739",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 31
      },
